      "content": "Wait, how can you say it's been \"correctly categorized and excluded\"? If that shipment is excluded from the EU total, then it's still part of our total inventory volume, right? \n\nIf the Tanjung Pelepas blades aren't counting toward the 60% EU requirement, then we have to be sourcing an even larger volume from Europe to compensate for them. That doesn't seem mathematically possible given our recent German supplier logs. \n\nCan you show me the specific math or the breakdown of how you're calculating that 62%? If we're excluding a huge chunk of our inventory from the \"EU\" side, the percentage should be dropping, not staying high. I need to see the logic behind that number before I sign off.",
